{"assets":["/statement-assets/14f5f1676a4aa9636bc24ed6db0625cb774127866302a883bfc6c127411be0a8.png","/statement-assets/d95725cc917f5ca42ac02febaaf6eb41e2ed667c4fef0afd0c786b1cf2af36f1.png","/statement-assets/7b38b14ca9d59c8f41bb147fddca49dd6ec143a649e3d001f9ca4df9fce2547e.png","/statement-assets/bfb1e8ccc68b5c738648b154d06a15ae03ec152886a23756ff3fc3accfcacba0.png","/statement-assets/425ed94ad8ce50a4f0cd8f8f8adeab0de667b5011a65dbe385c0d7320cb7005f.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1446","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Long Recovery"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A patient has been infected with an unknown disease. His body can be seen as an infinite grid of triangular cells which looks as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/14f5f1676a4aa9636bc24ed6db0625cb774127866302a883bfc6c127411be0a8.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Two cells are neighboring if they share a side. Therefore, each cell ($$$x$$$, $$$y$$$) has exactly three neighbors: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" ($$$x+1$$$, $$$y$$$) "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" ($$$x-1$$$, $$$y$$$) "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" ($$$x+1$$$, $$$y-1$$$) if $$$x$$$ is even and ($$$x-1$$$, $$$y+1$$$) otherwise. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Initially some cells are infected, all the others are healthy. The process of recovery begins. Each second, for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly one"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" cell (even though there might be multiple cells that could change its state) one of the following happens:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" A healthy cell with at least $$$2$$$ infected neighbors also becomes infected. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" An infected cell with at least $$$2$$$ healthy neighbors also becomes healthy. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If no such cell exists, the process of recovery stops. Patient is considered recovered if the process of recovery has stopped and all the cells are healthy."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We're interested in a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"worst-case"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" scenario: is it possible that the patient never recovers, or if it's not possible, what is the maximum possible duration of the recovery process?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer $$$n$$$ $$$(1 \\leq n \\leq 250000)$$$  — the number of infected cells. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The $$$i$$$-th of the next $$$n$$$ lines contains two space-separated integers $$$x_i$$$ and $$$y_i$$$ $$$(0 \\leq x_i, y_i \\lt 500)$$$, meaning that cell $$$(x_i, y_i)$$$ is infected. All cells $$$(x_i, y_i)$$$ are distinct, and all other cells are considered healthy. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is possible that the organism never fully recovers from the disease, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"SICK"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Otherwise, you should print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RECOVERED"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and in the next line an integer $$$k$$$  — the longest possible recovery period, modulo $$$998244353$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n0 0\n1 0\n2 0\n0 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nRECOVERED\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1 0\n3 0\n1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nSICK\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the first testcase, the following drawings describe the longest possible recovery process. It can be proven that there are no recovery periods of length $$$5$$$ or longer, and the organism always recovers in this testcase."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/d95725cc917f5ca42ac02febaaf6eb41e2ed667c4fef0afd0c786b1cf2af36f1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\hspace{40pt} \\downarrow$$$ "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/7b38b14ca9d59c8f41bb147fddca49dd6ec143a649e3d001f9ca4df9fce2547e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\hspace{40pt} \\downarrow$$$ "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/bfb1e8ccc68b5c738648b154d06a15ae03ec152886a23756ff3fc3accfcacba0.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\hspace{40pt} \\downarrow$$$ "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/425ed94ad8ce50a4f0cd8f8f8adeab0de667b5011a65dbe385c0d7320cb7005f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\hspace{40pt} \\downarrow$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\hspace{15pt}$$$ RECOVERED"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the second testcase, it is possible for the cells $$$(2, 0)$$$, $$$(2, 1)$$$, $$$(0, 1)$$$ to become infected. After that, no cell can change its state, so the answer is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"SICK"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", as not all of the cells are healthy."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1446E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1446/problem/E"}